    "title": "Why Snorkel AI Simulates Agents Instead of Replaying Traces",
    "source_text": "Why Snorkel AI Simulates Agents Instead of Replaying Traces.\nProduction traces show what an AI agent did on a single run, but they can't be replayed cleanly — database state, tool versions, and environments all shift, so A/B comparisons never test like for like. Snorkel AI converts those traces into offline, repeatable simulation benchmarks that mirror a company's own tools, APIs, policies, and workflows. Agent configurations can then be compared in parallel on cost, latency, and retry counts instead of pass rate alone.",
